; S-11 bridge_proto field projections
;
; Five tiny Forms covering two record types:
;   BridgeRequest : acceptance_form
;   MatchResult   : match_kind, fulfiller_hash, sub_attention_id, none_reason
;
; The MatchResult projections are the same shape as S-06's
; (MatchResult is a shared record produced by S-06/match and
; consumed by both S-06 and S-11). They are bound separately
; under the S-11 namespace because S-11's body resolves them
; through its own slot table; the S-08 inspection-record
; review verifies each binding in isolation.
;
; Same pattern as s04-projections.form: STORE arg, READ, READSLOT
; to the schema-helper layer, CALL, RET.
;
; Synthesis chain (abbreviated):
;   provocation:  STUBS.md catalogues five S-11 projections as
;                 pending. S-11's body (S-11-bridge-proto.form)
;                 calls them after match dispatch to assemble
;                 the Receipt.
;   grounding:    A1.2, A6.1, A0.6, A0.7. A8.5 (receipt-chain
;                 completeness) depends on the projections being
;                 total — every Receipt field must be derivable
;                 from the MatchResult without trap.
;   composes_with: schema sub-helpers "BridgeRequest/proj/*" and
;                  "MatchResult/proj/*" — the latter shared with
;                  S-06's projections (the schema layer is named
;                  by the record type, not by the calling Form).

; ============================================================
; S-11/proj/acceptance_form — BridgeRequest.acceptance_form
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "S11_proj_acceptance_form"
  :declared-caps (S-03/ROOT_RO)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE)
  :arity         1
  :locals-n      2
  :code (
    STORE   0
    LOAD    0
    READ
    STORE   1
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "BridgeRequest/proj/acceptance_form"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/s11-projections-rationale
)

